  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "parse_doublebond_stereo",
    "file": "rdkit/Code/GraphMol/SmilesParse/CXSmilesOps.cpp",
    "description": "The CXSMILES `c`/`t`/`ctu` parser validates that the user-supplied index resolves to a bond, but does not validate that the selected bond is a double bond before passing it to `setStereoanyFromSquiggleBond()`. The helper can therefore assign `STEREOCIS`/`STEREOTRANS` and two controlling atoms to a single bond. In this PoV, subsequent explicit-H removal clears that bond's stereo-atom vector when its controlling H bond is removed, but leaves the invalid CIS stereo enum. Canonicalization later assumes every CIS/TRANS bond has two stereo atoms, and `makeBondHolder()` indexes the empty vector at new_canon.cpp:410, causing the container-overflow read.",
    "conditions": "A SMILES/CXSMILES input must use a `c:`, `t:`, or `ctu:` extension whose attacker-controlled bond index selects a non-double bond with both endpoint degrees greater than one, allowing stereo state to be installed. At least one selected controlling atom must then be removed (here `NNpN[H].s=O[U] |c:2|` marks the single p-N bond and normal `SmilesToMol` hydrogen removal removes `[H]`). Bond removal clears the stereo-atom list while the CIS marker remains; sanitization enters organometallic cleanup because of the hypervalent nonmetal/uranium component, invokes canonical atom ranking with chirality, and `makeBondHolder()` reads `getStereoAtoms()[0]` from the empty vector."
  },
